# Retry policy

## Backoff

Delay before attempt $n$ is exponential with full jitter, capped at
$t_{max}$: ^backoff-formula

$$
t_n = U\bigl(0,\; \min(t_{max},\; b \cdot 2^n)\bigr)
$$

Full jitter rather than fixed backoff, because synchronized clients retrying on
the same schedule reproduce the outage they are retrying against.[^thundering]

[^thundering]: The failure mode is a thundering herd: every client backs off by
    exactly the same amount and returns in a single wave.

## Budget

A caller retries at most three times, and the total time spent retrying counts
against the original request deadline rather than extending it.
